The helper handles one square layer at a time. It writes the top, bottom, left, and right sides of that layer, then moves inward. After the matrix is ready, the rows are printed.

The separate center case is covered naturally when the remaining square has one row and one column.

```csharp
public class Solution
{
    public void Pattern22(int n)
    {
        int size = 2 * n - 1;
        int[,] grid = new int[size, size];

        FillLayer(grid, 0, size - 1, n);

        for (int row = 0; row < size; row++)
        {
            for (int col = 0; col < size; col++)
            {
                Console.Write(grid[row, col] + " ");
            }
            Console.WriteLine();
        }
    }

    private void FillLayer(int[,] grid, int start, int end, int value)
    {
        if (start > end)
        {
            return;
        }

        for (int col = start; col <= end; col++)
        {
            grid[start, col] = value;
            grid[end, col] = value;
        }

        for (int row = start; row <= end; row++)
        {
            grid[row, start] = value;
            grid[row, end] = value;
        }

        FillLayer(grid, start + 1, end - 1, value - 1);
    }
}
```

For `n = 3`, the first call fills the `5 x 5` outside border with `3`. The next call fills the inner border with `2`, and the final call puts `1` in the center.

Time complexity: `O(n^2)` including printing. Space complexity: `O(n^2)` for the matrix plus `O(n)` recursive calls.

This version prints one layer at a time. The first layer fills the outside square with `n`, then the next layer fills the inside square with `n - 1`. The loops stop after reaching the center.

The pattern is printed directly, so no matrix is needed.

