For `n = 3`, the size is `5`. The center cell has distance `2` from an edge, so its value is `3 - 2 = 1`.

Time complexity: `O(n^2)` because there are `(2n - 1)^2` cells. Space complexity: `O(1)`.

I used a matrix here instead of printing immediately. Each cell starts with its distance from the nearest edge. The outside cells get the largest number, and values decrease as the position moves toward the center.

This makes the output order easy to see, although the matrix takes extra memory.

