class Solution {
    public void pattern22(int n) {
        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
            boolean first = true;

            for (int j = 0; j < i + 1; j++) {
                if (!first) System.out.print(" ");
                System.out.print(n - j);
                first = false;
            }

            for (int j = 0; j < 2 * (n - i) - 3; j++) {
                if (!first) System.out.print(" ");
                System.out.print(n - i);
                first = false;
            }

            if (i != n - 1) {
                for (int j = 0; j < i + 1; j++) {
                    if (!first) System.out.print(" ");
                    System.out.print(n - i + j);
                    first = false;
                }
            } else {
                for (int j = 2; j < n + 1; j++) {
                    if (!first) System.out.print(" ");
                    System.out.print(j);
                    first = false;
                }
            }
            System.out.println();
        }

        for (int i = 1; i < n; i++) {
            boolean first = true;

            for (int j = 0; j < n - i - 1; j++) {
                if (!first) System.out.print(" ");
                System.out.print(n - j);
                first = false;
            }

            for (int j = 0; j < 2 * i + 1; j++) {
                if (!first) System.out.print(" ");
                System.out.print(i + 1);
                first = false;
            }

            for (int j = 0; j < n - i - 1; j++) {
                if (!first) System.out.print(" ");
                System.out.print(2 + i + j);
                first = false;
            }
            System.out.println();
        }
    }
}
```

## Complexity
**Time Complexity:**
O(n^2) The algorithm consists of two main outer loops, each running $n$ times. Inside these loops, the total number of print operations across the three inner loops always sums up to approximately $2n - 1$. Therefore, the total operations are proportional to $n \times (2n)$, resulting in quadratic time complexity. 

**Space Complexity:**
O(1) The solution prints the pattern directly to the console. It does not use any additional data structures (like 2D arrays) that scale with the input size $n$. Only a few integer variables and boolean flags are used.

